There is a robotic arm which is being fixed on a four wheeler car. The end of the robotic arm has a Capacitive Soil Moisture Sensor attached to it to check the moisture of the soil of the individual plant pot. 
The camera of the robotic arms see a plant plot and head towards it. The plant pots are usually give a tag using numbers for a reference point. When the car goes to the plant plot, it eventually stops at some distance. 
Now the camera captures the visual data and send it to the computing unit (Nvidia Jetson or Nvidia GPU) for the computing process. The Computer Vision Technology commands the ESP32 Dev Module to move the arm in order to penetrate the Moisture Sensor into the soil. There is a current measuring sensor in our system, if the Servo Motors increases the current input more than the threshold level then the robot assumes that the Soil to “too dry”, and the Computer Vision also conforms this by computing the visual data.
